# DRAGON QUEST V (Japan, Super Famicom): the codes of its dialogue, 16 bits each (written here high byte first).
# A code is the character's number in the dialogue's own font, in no order that helps. Each was read off the
# picture the game drew for it in play (a code leaving the game's queue, and the glyph it drew that frame), then
# in the sentences it stands in. Only characters met in play so far are here; the rest come out as U+FFFD.
